  "issue_number": 135,
  "issue_title": "fix: use QUERY transcript for cached pr_eval routing",
  "issue_body": "## Summary\r\n\r\nFixes a critical scoring mismatch: **cached hidden eval (70% of composite)** routed the coordinator on the bare benchmark prompt, while training and live eval always use the turn-1 `QUERY:\\n` transcript from `run_trajectory`.\r\n\r\n## Root cause\r\n\r\n`_evaluate_cached()` and `_compute_novelty()` called `encoder.encode(canonical[\"prompt\"])`. Every other path (`train`, `eval`, live `pr_eval`) builds coordinator input via `_transcript_text(query, [])` \u2192 `\"QUERY:\\n{prompt}\"`. Different tokenization \u2192 different hidden states \u2192 different routing decisions on the primary score component.\r\n\r\n## Fix approach\r\n\r\n- Add `_routing_transcript()` helper that delegates to `_transcript_text(prompt, [])`\r\n- Use it in `_evaluate_cached()` and `_compute_novelty()` before encoding\r\n\r\n## Impact\r\n\r\n- Cached hidden accuracy, overfit gate, and novelty now route on the same coordinator input miners train against\r\n- Complements open PR #5 (SVF scales); this PR is transcript-only and does not overlap\r\n\r\n## Tests\r\n\r\nAdded `tests/test_pr_eval_cached_transcript.py` (2 tests).\r\n\r\n## Risks / tradeoffs\r\n\r\n- Cached scores may shift for submissions evaluated under the old bare-prompt path. This aligns scoring with the documented training contract, not inflation.\r\n",
  "merged_at": "2026-07-11T04:09:01.000Z",
  "test_cmd": [
    "python",
    "-m",
    "pytest",
    "--tb=short",
    "-q",
    "tests/test_pr_eval_novelty.py"
  ],
